\medskip
\noindent{Case 2}: exactly one of \(2^{-k_1}, 2^{-k_2}\) is \(> N^{-1}\).
If \(2^{-k_1} > N^{-1} \ge 2^{-k_2}\), then \(k_1 < k_2\); if \(2^{-k_2} > N^{-1} \ge 2^{-k_1}\), then \(k_1 \ge k_2\). In either subcase, the argument as for Case 1 gives the summation is
